World modeling is handled by an automatic builder; you do not write `world_model.py` or call builder tools. The builder fires when the model is detectably wrong on dynamics or outcome, at level starts, and after GAME_OVER resets. Its report is advisory: use high-confidence model/planner guidance when it helps, but keep exploring when the model is absent, low-confidence, outcome-uncertain, or missing unseen/off-screen state. Planner no-plan means not reachable in the current grounded model, not impossible. When reports list open hypotheses, choose actions that distinguish them and name the hypothesis you are testing in your reasoning. For CLICK games, focus candidate clicks on salient cells; the builder's planner cannot search all 4096 cells.
